{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":15000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"gpt-6-luna","packSha":"a6ec6cc6a4d2ef60ef7fb86e715fba813f5b64c201c399dde421d4096673eb64","packTokens":1201,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"tpl","tokens":51,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spans","tokens":206,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"answers","tokens":485,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"sentences","tokens":404,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":6,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"Map each restated sentence to the original intent spans (I-n) and answers (Q-n) it comes from. A sentence that matches none gets empty lists. Every sentence n must appear once.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spans\" kind=\"intent\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-1\",\n  \"text\": \"Build every operation of the locked API contract in contracts/openapi.yaml, exactly as it is written there.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-2\",\n  \"text\": \"Keep the data in the project's PostgreSQL database (the connection string named App, which the project already reads).\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-3\",\n  \"text\": \"Write its sample data in App.Api/SeedData.cs: a few believable rows for each table, taken from the contract's examples, so each list has something to show.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-4\",\n  \"text\": \"The app runs that file only when the setting Seed:Demo is true, so no test may count on those rows.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-5\",\n  \"text\": \"The web app is built in its own repo; do not build screens here.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"answers\" kind=\"answers\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-1\",\n  \"question\": \"How many demo requests and what status/area coverage should SeedData.Run provide, given the product document specifies exactly eight but the implementation request asks for only a few contract-example rows?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Seed a few believable rows from the contract examples, without requiring eight rows or specified status and area counts.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-2\",\n  \"question\": \"What should happen if SeedData.Run is invoked more than once while demo seeding is enabled?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Do not insert duplicate demo rows on repeated runs.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-3\",\n  \"question\": \"For create-request validation, should the API implement only the validation and error details defined by the locked OpenAPI contract, or also enforce the product document’s explicit field limits and messages wherever they differ or are absent from the contract?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Use only the validation and errors defined by the locked OpenAPI contract.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"question\": \"If PostgreSQL is unreachable, should the application fail during startup, or start successfully and fail only when an operation needs the database?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Fail startup when PostgreSQL cannot be reached; do not fall back to another store.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-5\",\n  \"question\": \"Should the existing GET / health endpoint remain alongside the four contract operations, or should it be removed so the API exposes only the operations in the contract?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Keep the existing GET / health endpoint in addition to the four contract operations.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"sentences\" kind=\"restated\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"n\": 1,\n  \"text\": \"Implement the Maintenance Requests API so listing requests supports descending createdAt ordering, optional status filtering, and the specified 400 and 500 error responses.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 2,\n  \"text\": \"Implement request creation with schema validation, trimmed title and description, system-assigned id and UTC createdAt, Open status, omission of blank descriptions, and the specified success and error responses.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 3,\n  \"text\": \"Implement retrieval by id and status updates with the specified success responses, allowed status transitions, validation, not-found and conflict handling, and server-error responses.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 4,\n  \"text\": \"Persist request records in PostgreSQL selected by ConnectionStrings:App so they remain available after restart, and fail startup if PostgreSQL is unreachable without switching data stores.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 5,\n  \"text\": \"Implement an idempotent SeedData.Run method that seeds exactly one row for each of the three selected contract examples, and invoke it at startup if and only if Seed:Demo is true.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 6,\n  \"text\": \"Keep API-operation tests independent of demo rows, and do not add maintenance-request screens or pages to the API delivery; the screen-flow end-to-end test belongs in the separate web-app repository.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 7,\n  \"text\": \"Keep GET / returning HTTP 200 with the response body \\\"API is up\\\".\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\nMap the sentences."}